\import{dt-macros}
\import{ltp-macros}
\title{Obligation properties}
\taxon{Definition}
\meta{source}{(from [[manna-pnueli-1990]])}
\p{An \em{obligation} property is comprised of (finite) boolean combinations of [safety](ltp-0004) and [guarantee](ltp-0005) properties. That is:}
\ul{
\li{Every [guarantee](ltp-0004) property is an obligation property.}
\li{If #{P} is an obligation property, then #{\compl{P}} is an obligation property.}
\li{If #{P} and #{Q}  are obligation properties, then #{P \cap Q} is an obligation property.}
\li{If #{P} and #{Q}  are obligation properties, then #{P \cup Q} is an obligation property.}
}
\p{Topologically, this is called the \em{constructible sets} of our [topology](ltp-0007).}